Exact F5 identity: (1+3*zeta)^8=zeta², so the infinity collision is excluded.
Fermat cubic C(F5): [(0, 3, 1), (1, 1, 1), (2, 4, 1), (3, 0, 1), (4, 2, 1), (1, 4, 0)]
Rational fixed points of swapping u,v: [(1, 1, 1), (1, 4, 0)]
With P=(1,1,1) as origin, swap is inversion; the two finite cusps are outside C(F5)[2].
Hence their 3-primary Abel–Jacobi differences are nonzero; together with the unit test, all three cusps are separated from P.
The S3 action on U(F5) is transitive, so every interior point is separated from every cusp in the full geometrically pro3 group.
No claim of separation for every finite field, or of a collision at a passing row, is made.
